# These belong on the juiceworks-api Netlify site (Site configuration >
# Environment variables), alongside the CarrierCalc lead-capture vars. Copy to
# .env only for local `netlify dev`.
#
# NEVER commit real values. .env is gitignored; keep it that way. This
# repository is public.

# Fine-grained personal access token. Scope it as tightly as this:
#   Resource owner:         justindbilyeu
#   Repository access:      Only select repositories -> Tech-but-Verify
#   Repository permissions: Contents = Read and write
#                           (everything else = No access)
# If this token leaks it can write files to this one repo and nothing more.
# Revoke at https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_replace_me

# Where submissions are committed, as "owner/repo".
GITHUB_REPO=justindbilyeu/Tech-but-Verify

# Optional. Branch to commit to; defaults to the repo's default branch.
# GITHUB_BRANCH=main

# Optional. Overrides the allowed browser origin for CORS. Defaults to
# https://justindbilyeu.github.io plus localhost for `netlify dev`.
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://justindbilyeu.github.io

# Optional. Turns on per-crew-boss PINs: a JSON object mapping PIN to name.
# Unset (the current state) leaves the checklist open to anyone with the link.
#
# Set this AND flip PIN_REQUIRED to true in docs/index.html -- one without the
# other either adds a box nobody checks or rejects every submission.
#
# Use 6 digits, not 4, and read the PIN section of the README first: this is a
# speed bump against someone filing under the wrong name, not authentication.
# A set but malformed value fails closed -- submissions are refused rather than
# silently falling back to an open checklist.
# CREW_PINS={"481027":"John Smith","730914":"Ana Reyes"}
